  "prompt": "Mailvora's marketing manager reads sign-ups by first-touch source and medium from the export. Check November 2025 against the backend. On the export side, count the sign_up events of the Dublin days 1 to 30 November (by event_date), every one of them, grouped by traffic_source.source and traffic_source.medium, the visitor's first touch. On the backend side, count the signups whose signup_ts falls on those Dublin days, grouped by the utm_source and utm_medium of the visitor's first session (the earliest session_start of that visitor_id in sessions), with a missing utm_source read as (direct) and a missing utm_medium as (none). Return five columns, in this order: source, medium, export_signups, backend_signups and difference (export_signups minus backend_signups). Return one row for each source and medium that either side has, with 0 where a side has none. Any row order is fine.",
  "output_contract": {
